2.0.1:
[New] detect_run_mode() function for structured run-mode identification;
      returns watch/systemd, watch/init, watch/manual, timer/systemd,
      cron, or unknown
[Change] show_status() refactored to use detect_run_mode(); mode display
         now includes sub-type (systemd/init/manual) for watch mode and
         shows "no scheduler detected" for unknown mode
[New] tests/20-cli.bats: 6 tests for detect_run_mode() (cron, unknown,
      single-line output) and show_status display lines
[New] --verbose/-V global modifier flag for detailed output; stripped by
      pre-process loop alongside --json/--csv
[New] vout() verbose-only output function in bfd.lib.sh; prints to stdout
      when VERBOSE=1, returns 0 always; silenced by -q (exec redirect)
[New] verbose instrumentation in check() (per-rule events/threshold, filtered
      hosts, ban execution), process_unbans() (per-unban detail),
      show_status() (detection method), _hc_binaries() (binary paths)
[New] tests/29-verbose.bats: 13 tests for vout(), flag parsing, verbose
      output in show_status/health_check/process_unbans
[Change] rules/*: migrate all 34 rule files from $TLOG_PATH subprocess to
         in-process _rule_tlog() call; eliminates 34 fork+exec pairs per
         detection cycle
[Change] test_rule(): rewrite to use _TLOG_PASSTHROUGH instead of mktemp
         tlog script; no temp file creation, no chmod, no TLOG_PATH override
[Change] tests/21-rule-test.bats: update mock rule pattern and setup to match
         _rule_tlog() migration
[New] _rule_tlog(): in-process tlog wrapper for rule execution; replaces
      $TLOG_PATH subprocess with tlog_read() call; _TLOG_PASSTHROUGH variable
      for test_rule() passthrough mode
[New] TLOG_BASERUN variable in internals.conf for tracking file directory;
      fallback in files/bfd, pre() validation, reload_watch() refresh
[Change] _hc_state(): health check reports TLOG_BASERUN path instead of
         hardcoded tmp/ reference
[New] tests/14-tlog.bats: 6 _rule_tlog unit tests (delta, first-run,
      passthrough modes, missing file/baserun)
[Change] tlog getsize(): replace cat subprocess with read builtin for tracking
         file reads; matches tlog_read() pattern in bfd.lib.sh
[Change] tlog_read(): replace cat subprocess with read builtin for tracking
         file reads; matches tlog getsize() pattern
[Change] tlog: simplify growth condition from NOT-less-than AND NOT-equal to
         single greater-than test; aligns with tlog_read() in bfd.lib.sh
[Change] tlog: annotate vestigial PATH export with rationale (standalone
         subprocess invocation, cron.daily, manual use)
[Change] exclude.files: add header and inline comments grouping entries by source
         (APF, TCP wrappers, BFD ignore lists, cPanel/WHM/Plesk)
[Change] bfd-watch.service: add SyslogIdentifier=bfd-watch and TimeoutStopSec=15
[Change] bfd.service: add SyslogIdentifier=bfd
[New] tests/28-install-paths.bats: 16 tests for install.sh INSPATH/BINPATH sed
      replacement logic (source file presence, replacement correctness, no stray
      defaults, combined replacement, bash -n validity, exclude.files paths,
      conditional guard)
[Change] Dockerfiles: add COPY lines for bfd-watch.service, bfd.service, cron,
         cron.daily, install.sh (all 9) for install-path tests
[Fix] tlog getsize(): eliminate pre-create block and duplicate branches; single
      size read on first run prevents spurious delta output from double-read race;
      semantics now match tlog_read() in bfd.lib.sh
[Change] tlog/bfd.lib.sh: update convergence comments cross-referencing both
         implementations and documenting migration path
[New] thresholds.conf: centralized per-rule threshold management; colon-
      delimited KEY=VALUE format supporting TRIG, SKIP_ALERT, RULE_EMAIL;
      three-tier precedence: rule file > thresholds.conf > conf.bfd
[New] _load_thresholds(): parse thresholds.conf into associative arrays with
      root-ownership and permission safety validation; graceful degradation
      on missing file
[New] _apply_thresholds(): fill empty threshold variables from thresholds.conf
      after rule sourcing; integrated into check(), 6 display functions, and
      SIGHUP reload
[Change] rules/*: TRIG commented out in all 34 rule files; thresholds now
         managed centrally via thresholds.conf with rule-file uncomment override
[Change] importconf: migrate per-rule TRIG values from old rule files (pre-
         thresholds upgrade) or preserve existing thresholds.conf (post-
         thresholds upgrade)
[New] tests/27-thresholds.bats: 15 tests for _load_thresholds and
      _apply_thresholds (parsing, safety, precedence)
[New] tests/17-check-pipeline.bats: 2 precedence integration tests for
      thresholds.conf in the check() pipeline
[New] tests/25-importconf.bats: 2 migration tests for thresholds.conf
      (pre-thresholds rule TRIG extraction, post-thresholds preservation)
[Fix] importconf: add cleanup trap for temp files on interrupt (SIGINT/SIGTERM);
      removes mktemp and merge_conf intermediate files on EXIT/INT/TERM
[Note] EXIT_USAGE_ERROR constant: FALSE POSITIVE — EXIT_CONFIG_ERROR is
       semantically correct for unknown CLI options; adding a new constant would
       change exit codes (backward compat freeze)
[Fix] get_state(): PID liveness check — when lock is fresh but holder PID is
      dead (OOM, SIGKILL), clear and re-acquire instead of waiting for timeout;
      cron recovers from dead watch daemon within one cycle (~2 min)
[New] bfd-watch.init: SysVinit init script for CentOS 6 / Ubuntu 14.04;
      cross-distro support (RHEL /etc/init.d/functions, Debian
      /lib/lsb/init-functions, bare fallback); start/stop/restart/reload/
      status/condrestart actions; SIGHUP reload, graceful SIGTERM shutdown
[New] install.sh: SysVinit init script installation on non-systemd systems;
      auto-detects /etc/rc.d/init.d (RHEL) or /etc/init.d (Debian)
[New] install.sh: post-install watch mode recommendation with init-system-
      appropriate command (systemctl or service)
[Change] install.sh: BINPATH sed also updates init script when installed
[New] uninstall.sh: SysVinit init script cleanup — stop service, remove
      chkconfig/update-rc.d entries, clean pidfile and subsys lock
[Change] README/README.md: reframe watch mode as recommended primary mode;
         section 2.1 leads with watch mode, cron presented as automatic
         fallback; section 5.4 adds SysVinit service management examples
         and dead-PID recovery explanation; Quick Start includes watch mode
         enable step after configure
[New] tests/26-init-script.bats: 20 tests — init script structural checks
      (syntax, LSB/chkconfig headers, case actions, paths) and get_state()
      PID liveness lock tests (dead PID recovery, live PID blocking, stale
      timeout, missing PID file, lock dir without timestamp)
